Steps to produce "nand-dump.img" (nand whole flash dump) & "nand-dump.img.mbn" (partition table)

------------------------------------------------
I. produce "nand-dump.img" (nand whole flash image dump)

a. burn nand-single.img
	(IPQ) # tftpboot 0x42000000 nand-single.img
	(IPQ) # crc32 0x42000000 ${filesize}

	(IPQ) # nand erase 0x0 0x10000000

	(IPQ) # imgaddr=0x42000000 && source $imgaddr:script
	(IPQ) # reset

b. read out the the whole flash (data + OOB)
	(IPQ) # nand read.raw 0x50000000 0x0 0x20000
	(IPQ) # tftpput 0x50000000 0x10800000 nand-dump.img

ps.
  * in nand, a page composed of (0x800 Byte data + 0x40 Byte OOB).
  * a 256MB (0x10000000) nand
    . include 0x20000 pages
    . the raw data size will be (0x800 + 0x40) x 0x20000 = 0x10800000

------------------------------------------------
II. produce "nand-dump.img.mbn" (nand flash partiton table for nand programmer)

a. edit nand partition config file "gen-nand-dump-img-mbn.conf"
   please refer to "nand-partition.xml" in qca-chipcode .

b. run
   $ gen-nand-dump-img-mbn.sh gen-nand-dump-img-mbn.conf nand-dump.img.mbn

